ddraw: Add WINE_DDRAW_GDI_FALLBACK + fix white flicker
 on GDI blit

This patch does two things:

1. Add WINE_DDRAW_GDI_FALLBACK environment variable.
   When set to a non-zero value, ddraw_surface_update_frontbuffer() skips
   the wined3d blit path (which blits to WINED3D_LOCATION_DRAWABLE via
   glBlitFramebuffer) and always takes the existing GDI BitBlt fallback
   path instead.

   This is needed on stacks where blitting to the default framebuffer is
   unreliable -- notably zink-over-a-Vulkan-wrapper without DRI3 on
   Termux-X11, where glBlitFramebuffer with a Y-flip to GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER=0
   (the window) crashes inside the Turnip driver / wrapper layer.

   OpenGL applications are unaffected because they present via wglSwapBuffers
   (Mesa/zink WSI present path) and never call glBlitFramebuffer to the
   default framebuffer.

2. Fix the white flicker that the GDI fallback used to cause.

   The original GDI fallback called GetDC(NULL), which returns the DC of
   the desktop (root) window. The BitBlt then wrote game content to the
   root window at window-relative coordinates, while the application's
   own window (containing the X server's compositor-managed backbuffer)
   was drawn on top. The result was a per-frame white flash: every frame
   the game wrote to the root window, then the X compositor painted the
   app window (still showing its cleared/white backbuffer) on top.

   The fix prefers the application's swapchain window DC via
   GetDC(ddraw->swapchain_window). With the application window's own DC,
   the BitBlt writes into the application window's backbuffer at
   window-relative coordinates, which is exactly what the game expects.
   The X compositor then composites the (now-filled) app window normally,
   no white flash.

   Fallback to GetDC(NULL) is preserved for the legacy Deer-Hunter popup
   case documented in the comment above the function.

This patch supersedes quartz-vmr7-gdi-fallback.patch: the VMR7 GDI fallback
was a workaround at the quartz (DirectShow) caller level. With this patch,
the fallback lives inside ddraw itself, so ALL DirectDraw primary-surface
updates (Blt, BltFast, Flip, Lock, GetDC) benefit from the GDI path when
the env var is enabled.

The env var is read on every call (matching the existing
vmr7_use_gdi_fallback() pattern in quartz). The cost is negligible (one
getenv() per primary-surface update, typically once per frame).

A one-time FIXME is emitted so users know the fallback is active when
debugging with WINEDEBUG.

diff --git a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
index 1b351e7..d11d2ef 100644
--- a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@ HRESULT ddraw_surface_update_frontbuffer(struct ddraw_surface *surface,
     struct wined3d_texture *dst_texture, *wined3d_texture;
     struct ddraw *ddraw = surface->ddraw;
     HDC surface_dc, screen_dc;
+    HWND screen_dc_window;
     int x, y, w, h;
     HRESULT hr;
     BOOL ret;
@@ -177,11 +178,22 @@ HRESULT ddraw_surface_update_frontbuffer(struct ddraw_surface *surface,
     if (surface->palette)
         wined3d_palette_apply_to_dc(surface->palette->wined3d_palette, surface_dc);

-    if (!(screen_dc = GetDC(NULL)))
-    {
-        wined3d_texture_release_dc(wined3d_texture, surface->sub_resource_idx, surface_dc);
-        ERR("Failed to get screen DC.\n");
-        return E_FAIL;
+    /* Prefer the swapchain window DC over the desktop (root) DC so the blit
+     * lands inside the application window instead of being written to the
+     * desktop root window and then over-composited by the X server (which
+     * causes a white flicker on stacks without DRI3, e.g. Termux-X11 + zink).
+     * Fallback to GetDC(NULL) preserves the legacy Deer-Hunter popup behavior
+     * documented above. */
+    screen_dc_window = ddraw->swapchain_window;
+    if (!(screen_dc = GetDC(screen_dc_window)))
+    {
+        screen_dc_window = NULL;
+        if (!(screen_dc = GetDC(NULL)))
+        {
+            wined3d_texture_release_dc(wined3d_texture, surface->sub_resource_idx, surface_dc);
+            ERR("Failed to get screen DC.\n");
+            return E_FAIL;
+        }
     }

     if (read)
@@ -191,7 +203,7 @@ HRESULT ddraw_surface_update_frontbuffer(struct ddraw_surface *surface,
         ret = BitBlt(screen_dc, x, y, w, h,
                 surface_dc, x, y, SRCCOPY);

-    ReleaseDC(NULL, screen_dc);
+    ReleaseDC(screen_dc_window, screen_dc);
     wined3d_texture_release_dc(wined3d_texture, surface->sub_resource_idx, surface_dc);

     if (!ret)
